From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 23:31:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 111/117] Input: apple_z2: Report runtime read failures

Runtime SPI errors were ignored by the threaded IRQ handler, making
transport failures indistinguishable from empty interrupts.

Capture the packet-read result and report failures with rate limiting
while preserving the existing transfer lock.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 0560875aacd372aab447dfb0be9c286160c44494
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index 42e504e02..ab5b02a50 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -1142,13 +1142,18 @@ static int apple_z2_j172_init_writes_locked(struct apple_z2 *z2)
 static irqreturn_t apple_z2_irq(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct apple_z2 *z2 = data;
+	int error;
 
 	if (unlikely(!z2->booted)) {
 		complete(&z2->boot_irq);
 	} else {
 		mutex_lock(&z2->io_lock);
-		apple_z2_read_packet(z2);
+		error = apple_z2_read_packet(z2);
 		mutex_unlock(&z2->io_lock);
+		if (error)
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(&z2->spidev->dev,
+					     "runtime packet read failed: %d\n",
+					     error);
 	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
